  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nHigh clouds will thicken over the region before daybreak Saturday,\nwhich will keep highs generally between 65 to 70 degrees.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nA mid level short wave will move out of the mid Mississippi Valley \nSaturday night and across the Ohio Valley Sunday into Sunday night. \nThere remains some uncertainty as to how much moisture will be pulled\nup into our area ahead of this, with the NAM and GFS trending towards\nthe drier European and Canadian models which have been precip-free \nfor the last several runs. \n\nA deeper mid/upper level trough is forecast to progress east across \nthe central CONUS early next week, but there remains significant \ndifferences in the timing of this as well as the timing/placement/ \nstrength of any embedded short waves. As a result, a fair bit of \nuncertainty continues with the forecast through the second half of \nthe long term period so will still broad brush with chance pops.",
